# Top-level pins for the Python binding jobs: python.yml, ci.yml test-python,
# nightly.yml and bench_baremetal.yml.
#
# One file serves every Python and OS those jobs run on, and pip-compile drops
# a requirement whose environment marker is false on the machine that compiles.
# So every dependency that holds only on some Python or OS is listed here
# unconditionally, with an exact pin: a pure-Python wheel that is harmless where
# the marker is false. Any compile of this file, on any Python (Dependabot
# compiles on its own), then resolves the same package set, and
# scripts/check_release_workflow.py fails a .txt whose set differs.
#   colorama         pytest, Windows only
#   exceptiongroup   pytest, Python < 3.11
#   tomli            pytest and maturin, Python < 3.11
#   typing-extensions  exceptiongroup, Python < 3.13
# Compile it on the OLDEST Python in the python.yml matrix (3.8) anyway: pytest
# 8.4 needs Python 3.9+ and pytest 9 needs 3.10+, so pytest is pinned to the
# last series that supports 3.8, and typing-extensions to the last release that
# does (4.13.2). .github/dependabot.yml holds both back.
#
# Refresh recipe: docs/CI.md, "Hashed Python requirements".
maturin==1.15.0
pytest==8.3.5
colorama==0.4.6
exceptiongroup==1.3.1
tomli==2.5.0
typing-extensions==4.13.2
